    "rationale": "Unaccustomed exertion followed by tense swollen legs, bilateral peroneal nerve conduction block, and MRI showing convex bulging of the crural fascia with muscle edema/necrosis indicate acute exertional compartment syndrome; severe CK elevation and necrosis are downstream muscle injury, not the primary unifying process.",
